#: /Script/FGearPlugin.FGearVehicle:mResponseOverrides [MapProperty ToolTip meta-data]
msgctxt "UObjectToolTips,FGearVehicle:mResponseOverrides"
msgid "This only works with line & sphere tracing. By default all channel responses are set to blocked, if you want to modify a channel response you can add an override to this list."
msgstr "This only works with line & sphere tracing. By default all channel responses are set to blocked, if you want to modify a channel response you can add an override to this list."

#. Key:	FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed
#. SourceLocation:	/Script/FGearPlugin.FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed [FloatProperty DisplayName meta-data]
#: /Script/FGearPlugin.FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed [FloatProperty DisplayName meta-data]
msgctxt "UObjectDisplayNames,FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed"
msgid "Reverse Brake Speed"
msgstr "Reverse Brake Speed"

#. Key:	FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed
#. SourceLocation:	/Script/FGearPlugin.FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed [FloatProperty ToolTip meta-data]
#: /Script/FGearPlugin.FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed [FloatProperty ToolTip meta-data]
msgctxt "UObjectToolTips,FGearVehicle:mReverseBrakeSpeed"
msgid "If the vehicles intended moving direction does not match its velocity the vehicle will automatically brake when the current speed is above this value. For ex. the vehicle is in first gear but it is moving backwards, when you press the throttle it will engage the brakes for you. The same goes for the reverse gear. This will be disabled when zero."
msgstr "If the vehicles intended moving direction does not match its velocity the vehicle will automatically brake when the current speed is above this value. For ex. the vehicle is in first gear but it is moving backwards, when you press the throttle it will engage the brakes for you. The same goes for the reverse gear. This will be disabled when zero."

